# KVQ (QUALIFY the audit op, second job of the session): optimisation/ttnn-op/kv_region_read/kv_region_read_card.py on the four-card (1, 4) mesh INSIDE the window image tp4-serve-11,
# through the fabric step's kvread probe (scripts/ci/tp4_kv_read_probe.py, run from this checkout, read-only mount): ttnn.qwen_read_blocks against the whole-cache read, byte for byte, for one block,
# a run, scattered ids, a shuffled order and two runs, on a pool-sized cache (19,968 blocks, one KV head per chip, allocated as production allocates its KV); the program cache must not grow.
# It also times the whole read apart from its host unpack (the split the cost model still lacks) and the region read per block (what P1ab-LN's 120 minutes assume).
# READ: the run conclusion (the probe exits 0 only on PASS) and the greppable line 'KV_READ_PROBE verdict=PASS'. FAIL, NOT-MEASURED or an image without the graft = the audited prefix arms are NOT run:
# P1ab-LN, E1-LN and P1-CTLR NEED this job (a region read nobody checked can digest a subset of the heads and agree with itself, a false PASS on most of the KV). Everything else goes on.
# The box is the probe's own timeout (the workflow bounds the docker run by it): 30 minutes under the fabric step's 45.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the chained session pack (tp4-session-0808-jobs; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it). Names no rig, card, host or registry.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset fabric
C2_FABRIC_PROBE=kvread
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
C2_BOX_MINUTES=30
